# Publishing tokens for CSV Grid Editor.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored and excluded from the packaged VSIX. Never commit it,
# and never paste a token into any other file in this repository.
#
# The release workflow does not read this file. In CI the same values come
# from repository secrets of the same names, set under
# Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions.


# --- Visual Studio Marketplace -------------------------------------------
#
# Azure DevOps Personal Access Token used by `npm run publish:extension`.
#
# Create one at https://dev.azure.com:
#   1. User settings > Personal access tokens > New Token
#   2. Organization: All accessible organizations
#   3. Scopes: Custom defined, then Marketplace > Manage
#   4. Expiration: 90 days is the practical maximum worth using
#
# The token is shown once. It must belong to a user with rights on the
# `bash-365` publisher, which owns the published extension.
VSCE_PAT=


# --- Open VSX -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Token for open-vsx.org, the registry VSCodium and Gitpod use. Optional:
# leave empty to skip Open VSX publishing.
#
# Create one at https://open-vsx.org after signing in with GitHub:
#   Settings > Access Tokens > Generate New Token
OVSX_PAT=


# --- Overrides ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Publisher ID. Only set this if you are publishing under a different
# publisher than the one in package.json. Changing the publisher creates a
# separate Marketplace listing rather than updating the existing one.
# VSCE_PUBLISHER=bash-365
